.TH "INSPEKT\-AUTOCOMPLETE" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-autocomplete \- Check autocomplete attributes on form fields
per WCAG 2.1 SC 1.3.5.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]autocomplete\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check autocomplete attributes on form fields per WCAG 2.1 SC 1.3.5.
.PP
Analyzes all form fields (input, textarea, select) on the current page
and predicts appropriate autocomplete attributes using multi\-language
heuristics.
.PP
The check uses 7 matching strategies with weighted confidence scoring:
.IP \(bu 2
Label text (weight: 5) \- highest reliability
.IP \(bu 2
Placeholder text (weight: 4)
.IP \(bu 2
Name attribute (weight: 2)
.IP \(bu 2
ID attribute (weight: 2)
.IP \(bu 2
Field type (weight: 1)
.IP \(bu 2
Input type (weight: 1)
.IP \(bu 2
Form type (weight: 1) \- login vs signup detection
.PP
Supports multi\-language keyword matching (English, German, Dutch) with
fuzzy substring matching for robust field identification.
.PP
Fields are classified as:
.IP \(bu 2
violation: Missing or incorrect autocomplete (WCAG failure)
.IP \(bu 2
warning: Autocomplete might be needed but uncertain
.IP \(bu 2
pass: Correct autocomplete or not applicable
.SH ALIASES
Also available as: \f[B]inspekt ac\-check\f[R], \f[B]inspekt
wcag\-135\f[R].
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enthreshold\f[R], \f[I]FLOAT\f[R]
Minimum confidence (0\-1) to consider autocomplete required (default:
0.5)
.TP
\f[B]\(eninclude\-hidden\f[R]
Include hidden input fields in analysis
.TP
\f[B]\(eninclude\-disabled\f[R]
Include disabled input fields in analysis
.TP
\f[B]\(enjson\f[R]
Output results as JSON
.TP
\f[B]\(entimeout\f[R], \f[I]FLOAT\f[R]
Execution timeout in seconds (default: 30)
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
inspekt autocomplete
inspekt autocomplete \-\-confidence\-threshold 0.7
inspekt autocomplete \-\-include\-hidden \-\-include\-disabled
.EE
